   S~S  SimpleSal documents: metadata describing all of the documents in the template-docs repo

=====================

   S~S  What is the context that this description exists within?

------------------------------------------

   The SimpleSal/workspace-model repository contains a suggestion for the location of files.

   The template-docs repo's managed object files use the model's vocabulary to describe metadata.

   The workspace model describes the directory structure; the template docs describe the files.

------------------------------------------

   This repo root README is about the template-docs repo managed object files: README/RELEASE/etc.

   * the content is suggested by TSC LLC for descriptions of TSC LLC repositories, in template form.

   * minimal suggestions, ideas, documentation about the use and content of the metadata files.

   SimpleSal is a small boat trying to exist in the middle of the busiest harbors in the world.

   Local rules will always apply.

=====================

  S~S   SimpleSal explains the managed object concept

    TSC LLC's idea of a managed object: anything present in the repo that is NOT human metadata.

    The human metadata and the managed object, together, are what TSC LLC calls the "repo object".

        The repo database MANAGER application or user interface:

            transfers repo objects into and out of the repo database.
            maintains and shares repo metadata about the repo object.

        The repo database OWNER:

            maintains human metadata files describing the managed object.
            transfers human metadata and/or managed object content into and out of the repo database.
            invents conventions to separate the managed object from the metadata.

        The repo database USER:

            understands repo and human metadata well enough to find the correct managed object.
            transfers managed object content into and out of the repo database.
            may be a developer who simply copies files when directed or refers to common files,
                 the source of the version controlled files must be managed for them, by someone.

    Notice that version control systems are just databases of the differences between files.

------------------------------------------

   S~S  What are the contents of this repository?

    TSC LLC's chosen publishing style:

        1) the repo contains human metadata text files and the managed object as defined here;

        2) the conventions followed for separating the metadata are adopted from GITHUB. and LINUX.;

        3) the managed object is a single subdirectory in the root of the repository.


   The trick is that the information about authoring a metadata file is found within a metadata file.

------------------------------------------

   S~S  What happens in my workspace as a result of interacting with this repository?

    The managed object will be placed into your workspace, along with the human metadata file
    (depending on your ability to configure the repo App to only consider files matching filters).

    The only reason to have a copy locally is if these files are being modified for a release.
    Readers still awake will realize the SimpleSal metadata about the directory content will
    match the name and therefore overwrite a conventional software package's local metadata files.
    This is a disadvantage resulting from TSC LLC separating the managed object into a subdirectory.

------------------------------------------

